  "repair_or_experiment_note": "# V20 actual evaluation V22 and full-state V21 continuation\n\nThe human selected the original SCUT standing-ascent recipe, replacing the custom RL+BPTT branch. The original flat PPO has completed 283 of the intended 8000 iterations; rough PPO has not started. MOD4v1 hardware, PD/DC, full D0–D7, 400/100/50Hz, 2.5ms TGS32/4, 10mm closure episode reset and original canonical budget remain explicit adaptations.\n\nV20 full final is 8,923,888B SHA4b6255e6f9f3bf15ccfe5f65b02015dae990f7f9ab61ae7e6d4ced61b4197d13. Its original owner closed safely, waited its children, settled original cost and released leases. Its original postround evaluation failed on a missing required pose-cache receipt callback before actor construction/read; that error evaluated zero episodes and is retained. It is separate from the actual skill result below.\n\nIndependent V22 read the same final once, used the same original frozen actor/done, 80 first episodes, seed9137, 500 controls/10s and 200mm four-sided course. It completed 0/80 strict, zero whole-footprint cases, zero both-wheel top-support cases and maximum actual400Hz top force zero. 77 terminated, three reached10s; mean3.3265s, median2.43s. The current model reviewed four actual recorded pose sequences from side/top and the actual400Hz curves. All80 measured roots fell below .25m; selected env0/1/40/41 did so at .1600–.1625s, subsequently near .18m with substantial nonwheel support, before approaching the step edge. Selected lower-of-two wheel bottoms peaked only .081–.116m. This is failure to maintain standing/approach, not evidence of a deliberate route planner avoiding stairs. The frozen baseline snapshot lacks detailed termination reason masks, so do not label all77 orientation failures. World XY differs from commanded body-forward direction because initial yaw is randomized.\n\nThe original saved SCUT action clipping is null. Actual active action abs99 percentiles were approximately[1.70,1.16,2.08,1.01,3.09,3.12]. The other chat's clip6 repair is not inserted here. The confirmed source mismatch is a misplaced debug-counter increment in observation caching. Original flat disables debug and advances this counter only at reward tail when enabled. V21 restores that lifecycle; its contribution to baseline skill failure has not been causally isolated.\n\nV21 source clock CPU fixture passed against the actual old frozen reward class and original SCUT function. New synthetic realRSL24-control/20Adam update full-state roundtrip passed actor/critic/STD/allAdam equality, LR, global/named command/physical RNG and a single fresh reset. No production checkpoint was opened for CPU validation. New complete saves include scalar reward counters. LegacyV20 omitted them, so migration explicitly uses debug0/common6792; exact missing legacy clock continuation is not claimed. All original physical components/queues and streams are restored before one fresh physical episode; PhysX state itself is not resumed.\n\nV21 run MOD4_STANDING200_SCUT_RECIPE_V21_FLAT_1793728481083581300 is actually running on72GPU0. Original owner1556103/create1793728548.28, worker1556112/create1793728549.29; exact executable/argv are in the handoff. GO2026-11-04T01:55:48.998150+08; save02:55:48.998150; nominal03:00:48.998150. Source17Adam states all5660 and adaptiveLR.0012974633789062506 restored, same actor/critic/STD and all source learning tensors verified equal in the single necessary production decode. FIRST completed iteration284, 24controls/98304onpolicy samples/192physics, 20optimizerupdates, finite nonzero gradients, full save8,927,449B SHAe204a3fd814b76d7e1ab3c5509caa4211c581e33de34089b83d2c91fd40f886e. This proves actual resumed PPO, not stair skill. No restart/hotpatch/extra FIRST or model validation is needed.\n\nThe same original owner performs full save, safe training close and immediate independent80 evaluation. New evaluator fixes callback/pre-reset target capture and records closure/mimic/numerical/raw-observation flags. On actual owner exit and localserialFREE, use scut_recipe_v21/control.py closed once, render only recorded poses via scut_recipe_v18/render.py and review natively. Continue original flat toward8000 before original rough weights-only/freshAdam. No additional budget/reserve, old-once replay or other-scope operation.\n\nAll four4090 were read before production:72both empty,210empty but home filesystem578457600B free,86compute occupied. These are historical snapshots, not present availability. SSH clients closed and original session restored after inventory, launch and FIRST collection. Full final/evaluation/video/NPZ/media remain external and are indexed by actual path, bytes and already-published SHA; no model read or physics is run for Git.\n\nThe previous source-clock annotated trial remains a99d27ada6eb504fb6ecfc93003f1f12f5afec63/peeled84137c65824b0cac3be504e20e1c8e4924b88661. The new actualV20evaluation/V21production evidence receives its own unique stage record; later supplements reuse those objects. Old raw errors, all historical tags/peels and lqr5848b45a99b8c32af02eb61b507c3f95ab39e4ad remain protected. Intermediate source lookup errors were local read-only lookups, resolved using exact SHA historical Git sources; no production retry followed those lookups.\n",
